This is a clear gap. The strip_ansi_codes function only handles CSI sequences (ESC [) but doesn't handle:
1. OSC sequences (ESC ]...ST) — used by terminal hyperlinks (OSC 8), window titles, etc. rustc and cargo now emit OSC 8 hyperlinks for error codes. These leak through as garbage text into the model context.
2. Simple two-char escape sequences (ESC ( B, ESC ) 0, etc.) — character set selection

The OSC one is most impactful because cargo outputs like `\x1b]8;;https://doc.rust-lang.org/...\x1b\\error[E0308]\x1b]8;;\x1b\\` would currently leave the URL and control characters in the output.

