OK, now I have a solid understanding. Let me focus on the **most impactful improvement**: enhancing strip_ansi_codes to handle OSC sequences (Operating System Commands), which are increasingly common in modern terminal output. 

rustc 1.80+ and cargo now emit OSC 8 hyperlinks for error codes like:
```
\x1b]8;;https://doc.rust-lang.org/error_codes/E0308.html\x1b\\error[E0308]\x1b]8;;\x1b\\
```

The current strip_ansi_codes only handles CSI (`ESC [`) sequences, so these OSC sequences leak through into the compressed tool output that gets sent to the model context, wasting tokens and potentially confusing the model.

